  "privacyNoAccountsTitle": "No accounts",
  "privacyNoAccountsBody": "There is no sign-in. Ringgit Radar does not ask for your name, email or phone number, and it has no ads and no analytics.",
  "privacyDeviceTitle": "Your Wish List stays on your device",
  "privacyDeviceBody": "Your Wish List, your theme and language choices and the \"Show all titles\" setting are saved on this device only: in the browser's local storage on the web, in the app's preferences on Android. When you open your Wish List, the app asks our server for those games by their ids, so the server receives the ids in that request to answer it. It does not keep them or link them to you.",
  "privacyLogsTitle": "What our server logs",
  "privacyLogsBody": "Our server writes no access log. It logs only errors, for example a database error, and those lines hold an error message, not your address. To stop one visitor from overloading it, the server counts requests per internet address, in memory only. Those addresses are never written to disk.",
  "privacyPicturesTitle": "Pictures come from Nintendo's image server",
  "privacyPicturesBody": "Game art and screenshots load straight from the store's image server (img-eshop.cdn.nintendo.net). Your browser or phone asks it for each picture, so Nintendo receives your internet address and the usual details of a request, under Nintendo's own privacy policy. Ringgit Radar does not keep or pass on any pictures.",
  "privacyOthersTitle": "Who else sees your visit",
  "privacyOthersBody": "The site and its server run on Vercel. Vercel keeps request logs under its own policy, which can include the page you asked for, the time, your internet address and your browser type. Price data is stored with Supabase; it holds game prices and nothing about visitors, and it only ever hears from our server. Apart from those pictures, the web version loads everything, fonts included, from our own address, and the Android app talks only to our server.",
  "privacyNotNintendoTitle": "Not Nintendo",
  "privacyNotNintendoBody": "Ringgit Radar is an independent, unofficial app. Not affiliated with or endorsed by Nintendo. Prices are collected from the Malaysian Nintendo eShop and shown with their history; to buy a game, use your Switch.",
